274
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,220
How is she alive?

275
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:19,460
Our mistake.

276
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:22,839
We shouldn't have assumed
she'd go down that easily.

277
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:25,900
She's trying to get out!

278
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,860
Maybe it's too deep and she's stuck?

279
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:36,940
Then let's run while we still can! Agreed.

280
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,375
We don't have to win.

281
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:39,853
We just have to escape.

282
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:45,267
I'm afraid that won't
keep her busy for long.

283
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:48,762
Jinbei's right!

284
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:49,821
That's not good.

285
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:02,340
Her hunger pangs won't
subside on the road.

286
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,040
There's no stopping her.

287
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:08,340
There's my king!

288
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,920
Hurry, run!

289
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:20,660
Oh no, the ground's giving way!

290
00:20:22,520 --> 00:20:23,920
Get ready!

291
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:34,180
Bring me my wedding cake!

292
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,720
I know you have it!

293
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,540
You have my cake!

294
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:44,780
Give it to me!

295
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,940
She's climbing out.

296
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:57,240
Straw Hats, up here.

297
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,317
Pudding, Siobhan?

298
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,320
Pudding, what'd you want?

299
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:03,357
Are you here to trick us again or what?

300
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:05,617
You can stop Mama's
hunger pangs with my help.

301
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:06,637
It's an obvious trap.

302
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:09,017
I knew I should have tied
her up in the first place.

303
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:10,817
Please just listen to me!

304
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:12,977
Hold up, but why is Siobhan with her?

305
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:15,180
I thought she ran off with Benji.

306
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:16,337
I want to start...

307
00:21:16,420 --> 00:21:17,250
Like me!

308
00:21:17,333 --> 00:21:18,180
Would you shut up?

309
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,478
Just let me finish.

310
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,740
Oh, my dear Pudding, you're okay.

311
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:25,300
Your pretty little face is unharmed.

312
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:26,260
I'm so happy.

313
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:29,820
Get it together, Pudding.

314
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:36,980
Hurry, Big Mom's closing in.

315
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:41,060
Mama, get to the point before
everyone here ends up dead.

316
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,320
You're useless!

317
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:46,520
You deserve death, you miserable idiots!

318
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:48,050
Huh?

319
00:21:48,133 --> 00:21:49,840
Even if you do make it out to sea,

320
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:52,257
Mama will hunt your
crew down in cold blood

321
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:54,987
and watch you all sink
into the murky depths!

322
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:58,820
Hey, what did you just say?

323
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:01,480
Wrong, pudding!

324
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,277
What are you talking about?

325
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,600
What am I saying?

326
00:22:05,020 --> 00:22:07,197
You're right, you're right, I'm sorry!

327
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:11,080
Listen, Mama believes that you
guys stole her big wedding cake.

328
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:15,340
She's completely fixated on
that idea right now. Huh?

329
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:16,980
There is no cake.

330
00:22:17,120 --> 00:22:18,120
We don't have it.

331
00:22:18,220 --> 00:22:19,260
Yes, I know.

332
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:20,756
But as of right now,

333
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:22,737
Mama would chase you to
the ends of the world

334
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:25,257
just to get one bite
of that sweet dessert.

335
00:22:25,340 --> 00:22:27,140
Exactly. Give up, Sanji.

336
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:31,500
Come stand at my side and savor
this momentous occasion with me.

337
00:22:31,740 --> 00:22:34,564
We'll watch your friends
perish in Mama's hands.

338
00:22:39,540 --> 00:22:40,960
What is your deal?

339
00:22:41,380 --> 00:22:42,920
Would you cut that out?

340
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:44,037
I'm ruining the plan.

341
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:45,200
I'm such a wreck.

342
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:48,777
If you came here to torture
us, you can get lost, you jerk.

343
00:22:48,860 --> 00:22:49,690
Wait a minute.

344
00:22:49,773 --> 00:22:50,680
That's not it.

345
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:53,080
Hey, black-legged Sanji. Go ahead.

346
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:57,117
Not for nothing, but Pudding told me
you're really good at making sweets.

347
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,030
Uh-huh.

348
00:22:58,113 --> 00:23:00,460
But I'm first class at anything I make.

349
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,042
That's perfect.

350
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:04,257
Then you have to help us bake a cake.

351
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:07,260
The exact one Mama wants
so we can stop her.

352
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:11,980
Then we'll help all of you guys
escape. But why? You were free.

353
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:14,788
Because I still owe you
one for saving Lola.

354
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,160
I'll risk my life to repay you.

355
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:20,160
No complaints. Thanks a ton. Uh-huh.

356
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:21,550
Ha!

357
00:23:21,633 --> 00:23:23,117
Who knows if we'll survive or not.

358
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,537
But I'll make one thing clear.

359
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:26,280
I'm not doing this for you.

360
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:31,252
It's sheer luck that the cake I wanted
to bake is the same one Mama craves.

361
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:34,257
And I just passed by
this area by coincidence.

362
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:36,752
I didn't know you people would be around.

363
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:40,077
So don't go thinking I
came all the way here to

364
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,597
stop her because I didn't
want to see you all die,

365
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:44,860
you understand me? Sanji!

366
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:54,200
She's all over the place!

367
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:56,520
Anyway, back to business.

368
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:58,597
So where can we bake this cake?

369
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:01,974
All the ingredients we need
can be found in Chocolatown.

370
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:04,977
The plan is for the
three of us to head there

371
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:07,884
immediately and bake the
cake as fast as we can.

372
00:24:08,260 --> 00:24:12,080
Then we'll carry it back by boat
and pass it to the Straw Hats.

373
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:15,811
That should get it to Mama,
who will no doubt be after you.

374
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:19,759
The cake will serve as a diversion.

375
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:23,197
You'll just have to hold out
until we're finished baking.

376
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:24,110
Is that her?

377
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:30,897
Be warned that once you set
sail, enemies will swarm you.

378
00:24:30,980 --> 00:24:33,937
But I have faith that you'll
be able to pull through.

379
00:24:34,020 --> 00:24:34,850
We will.

380
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:35,950
Okay, then.

381
00:24:36,033 --> 00:24:36,980
I'll go with you.

382
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:38,190
Perfect.

383
00:24:38,273 --> 00:24:39,103
Hop on, quickly.

384
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:40,640
Hang on a second.

385
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:43,937
Who said I was giving you
a lift, you pathetic dummy?

386
00:24:44,020 --> 00:24:44,850
No.

387
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:47,560
I can't!

388
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,586
Big Mom, get out of the hole.

389
00:24:58,120 --> 00:24:59,414
We're counting on you,

390
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:01,277
because I don't think anything short of a

391
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:04,007
perfect cake will put
an end to this rampage.

392
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:09,800
Okay then, I'm going to leave you guys
for now, but I promise I'll be back.

393
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:13,830
Yeah!

394
00:25:16,660 --> 00:25:17,800
You got this!

395
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:19,280
I'm not worried!

396
00:25:27,840 --> 00:25:30,080
Hey, Pony, ship on!

397
00:25:34,040 --> 00:25:35,740
She's doing it again!

398
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:40,520
Get away!

399
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:46,660
You wanna tell me what the
two of you are doing here?

400
00:25:47,260 --> 00:25:49,640
Luffy, I'll meet up with you and see!

401
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:51,846
That wasn't a promise, Sanji!

402
00:25:55,700 --> 00:25:57,100
Ikaku!

403
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:42,957
You're kidding me?

404
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:44,837
That was too close for comfort.

405
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:46,917
Everyone, can you stand?

406
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:47,897
Let's go.

407
00:26:47,980 --> 00:26:50,156
We gotta hurry back to the Sunny now.

408
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:54,151
Wait, that's not the way.

409
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:57,828
Robin, go back down again.

410
00:26:58,140 --> 00:27:01,417
Head to where we were before, then
fly straight for the coastline.

411
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:02,330
Roger that.

412
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:05,580
Hey, Straw Hats!

413
00:27:06,620 --> 00:27:07,717
That's not the way.

414
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:09,757
You're all headed straight into a wall.

415
00:27:09,840 --> 00:27:10,740
Hold on a sec.

416
00:27:11,100 --> 00:27:12,688
Are you nice, Pudding, now?

417
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:15,137
I was certain we were
headed towards the sea.

418
00:27:15,220 --> 00:27:18,400
I suppose we've been fooled
yet again. Follow me.

419
00:27:18,620 --> 00:27:19,914
The coast is this way.

420
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:21,100
Okay, let's go!

421
00:27:22,760 --> 00:27:24,020
You'll never leave!

422
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:28,280
Let me handle this for you.

423
00:27:29,540 --> 00:27:30,820
Memory filament!

424
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:40,860
And now, flashbacks!

425
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:47,500
Oh yeah, I've got some
groceries to pick up.

426
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:51,637
My big brother bust me in the head.

427
00:27:51,720 --> 00:27:53,637
Wanna go for walkies, good girl!

428
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:56,017
I haven't seen my son in three weeks.

429
00:27:56,100 --> 00:27:57,700
Oh, where could he be?

430
00:27:58,620 --> 00:27:59,897
What's going on here?

431
00:27:59,980 --> 00:28:01,577
We must use this to our benefit.

432
00:28:01,660 --> 00:28:02,660
Let's hurry!

433
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:04,300
What happened?

434
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:08,697
Memories from the soul's original owners
have come flooding back to the homies.

435
00:28:08,780 --> 00:28:11,817
But just as a warning, the
effects won't last forever, okay!

436
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:15,657
While they're confused, they will
no longer be under mama's control.

437
00:28:15,740 --> 00:28:19,697
So your crewmates and other allies
can get out of the forest safely now.

438
00:28:19,780 --> 00:28:20,610
That's clever.

439
00:28:20,693 --> 00:28:21,900
Nice work, Pudding

440
00:28:25,500 --> 00:28:26,580
The hell?

441
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:29,016
How long have you been there, Sanchi?

442
00:28:30,420 --> 00:28:31,760
Not long, I guess

443
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:33,537
What?

444
00:28:33,620 --> 00:28:34,740
Didn't you notice?

445
00:28:35,580 --> 00:28:41,080
Anyway, let's head to Chocolat Town and
make this cake Get off and swim, you idiot!

446
00:28:41,660 --> 00:28:44,366
Your eyes are beautiful
even when you're angry

447
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:48,790
Huh?

448
00:28:48,873 --> 00:28:49,740
You gonna be okay?

449
00:28:50,580 --> 00:28:51,410
I'm fine!

450
00:28:51,760 --> 00:28:53,348
Don't pull that crap on me!

451
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:56,146
Or else I'll wring your
neck next time, Sanji!

452
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:57,390
Honey!

453
00:29:02,940 --> 00:29:06,000
All right, I see the coast
up ahead! Let's hurry!

454
00:29:06,340 --> 00:29:07,458
We're almost there.

455
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:11,097
Hey, do you Karoo think Pudding
is really on our side now?

456
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:12,177
Well, I'm unsure,

457
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:16,613
but we'd better not let our guard down
until we're out of their territory.

458
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:23,700
You'll die here.

459
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:26,320
Come on, Zeus.

460
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:28,896
What the hell's gotten into you, huh?

461
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:37,597
Why'd you go and attack us, you big dummy?

462
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:41,500
I'm sorry, but I didn't really
have a say in the matter.

463
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:44,137
I don't want to hear your dumb excuses.

464
00:29:44,220 --> 00:29:47,217
Don't ever let me catch you
doing that again. Right.

465
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:48,880
I heard you. Jeez.

466
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:51,816
That lightning cloud shirt was tasty.

467
00:29:52,100 --> 00:29:54,600
I'd love to get another nibble. Huh?

468
00:29:54,940 --> 00:29:58,357
You've been back a whole two minutes
and you're losing it already.

469
00:29:58,440 --> 00:30:00,200
Don't disobey Mama again.

470
00:30:00,860 --> 00:30:01,880
I know.

471
00:30:05,300 --> 00:30:06,800
Get over here.

472
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:12,300
Give. Me. Back. My. Wedding. Cake. Now!

473
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:13,840
Watch out!

474
00:30:16,420 --> 00:30:17,820
Everyone get down!

475
00:30:24,580 --> 00:30:25,980
What a pain!

476
00:30:26,460 --> 00:30:28,600
That attack nearly got us!

477
00:30:28,860 --> 00:30:30,684
Thank you for the save, Jinbei!

478
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:53,380
You were quite effective against
the Chess Peacekeepers, Skeleton.

479
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,640
Did you just catch on?

480
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:59,300
I'm the Soul King, baby.

481
00:31:00,140 --> 00:31:01,300
The Mirror.

482
00:31:01,700 --> 00:31:03,876
That's where they're all coming from.

483
00:31:06,380 --> 00:31:08,437
It's from Nami and Robin's room.

484
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:11,097
You think they'll get mad if we break it?

485
00:31:11,180 --> 00:31:13,137
Let's ask for forgiveness later.

486
00:31:13,220 --> 00:31:14,957
Shatter it to pieces!

487
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:19,037
And who exactly are you
going to apologize to?

488
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:22,177
You did see the lightning
earlier, didn't you?

489
00:31:22,260 --> 00:31:25,297
Your crew is on its last lickety leg.

490
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:30,857
You know it's not too lickety

491
00:31:30,940 --> 00:31:32,557
late to take me up on that offer.

492
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:35,797
I made no matter how hard
you try you'll never be

493
00:31:35,880 --> 00:31:38,497
able to keep up with our
endless droves of soldiers.

494
00:31:38,580 --> 00:31:42,377
You'll collapse long before the waves
stop pouring out of that mirror.

495
00:31:42,460 --> 00:31:45,757
I'm not an unreasonable man though.

496
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:48,820
Submit now and I'll at
least spare your life.

497
00:31:49,420 --> 00:31:50,897
Your friends are dead.

498
00:31:50,980 --> 00:31:52,117
Let it go already.

499
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:56,060
Are you done talking to yourself yet?

500
00:31:57,380 --> 00:31:59,017
What a foolish question!

501
00:31:59,100 --> 00:32:01,840
I am tired of repeating myself.

502
00:32:03,040 --> 00:32:05,777
I'll ask you once again
to get off this ship.

503
00:32:05,860 --> 00:32:08,880
The Sunny belongs to
the Straw Hat Pirates.

504
00:32:10,300 --> 00:32:13,740
You're absolutely certain you
want to go down this path?

505
00:32:27,940 --> 00:32:29,157
Very well, then.

506
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:33,534
Who am I to complain if my enemies
don't happen to value their own lives?

507
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:38,280
Since you're begging me, I shall give
you both the sweet taste of death.

508
00:32:48,220 --> 00:32:51,000
We can head straight to Kaku Island now!

509
00:32:58,400 --> 00:32:59,900
Brooke! Chopper!

510
00:33:00,220 --> 00:33:02,380
Wait a minute, isn't that your ship?

511
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,877
Damn it, it looks like
they're getting attacked.

512
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:07,078
They set up an ambush woefully fast.

513
00:33:07,780 --> 00:33:10,420
Oh no, my big brothers are there!

514
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:15,180
They must be targeting Sanji's crewmates.

515
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:18,800
That'll teach ya!

516
00:33:19,060 --> 00:33:20,354
Your friends are dead!

517
00:33:20,460 --> 00:33:22,897
They were no match for
my darling brothers.

518
00:33:22,980 --> 00:33:25,977
You shouldn't have let those
weaklings defend for themselves.

519
00:33:26,060 --> 00:33:31,677
fool really back there pudding i can't

520
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:34,172
believe i actually said all that out loud

521
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:38,577
and what do you want to do
should we drop you off down

522
00:33:38,660 --> 00:33:42,437
there it's fine more important

523
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:46,537
for me to help you all right

524
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:49,637
if you're sure we'll just keep
on moving forward then the

525
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:53,177
thing about my friends is You
don't need to worry about them

526
00:33:53,260 --> 00:33:56,140
Knowing those guys, they'll be just fine

527
00:33:58,560 --> 00:34:03,140
So let's do this we're gonna
knock out big mom with this cake
